# Package set installed by install.sh when running under WSL.
#
# Inclusive, not subtractive: this file REPLACES packages/pacman and
# packages/yay on a WSL host. Whatever is not listed here is not installed.
# Entries that come from the AUR must also appear in packages/yay — that is
# how install.sh knows to route them through yay instead of pacman.
#
# packages/cargo, packages/package.json and packages/requirements.txt are not
# filtered; every entry in those works unchanged under WSL.
#
# The desktop here is sway on the wlroots headless backend, exported over VNC
# by wayvnc (see wsl.sh) rather than WSLg. That is a real Wayland session with
# Linux-side rendering, so compositor, fonts, themes and input method all
# belong here. Only things that need hardware the WSL VM does not have, or a
# compositor it cannot run, are left out — see the tail of this file.

